WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.818
Find continuity at 1
The function equals x squared minus one divided by x minus one when x differs
from one. At one, it has an unknown assigned value a.

2
00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:27.818
Write the condition
For continuity, the value at one must equal the limit. Start by calculating
the limit using the expression defined near this point.

3
00:00:27.818 --> 00:00:41.727
Simplify for x ≠ 1
Factor the difference of squares. The numerator becomes x minus one times x
plus one. Cancel the common factor because x differs from one.

4
00:00:41.727 --> 00:00:54.273
Calculate the limit
As x approaches one, x plus one tends to two. This is the limit that the
function's assigned value must match.

5
00:00:54.273 --> 00:01:10.000
Conclude
Therefore a must be two. We have filled the gap with the appropriate value.
Remember that the limit and the value at the point must agree for continuity.
